        "id": 1002790
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-27T08:03:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks, you\u0027re right that the board shouldn\u0027t need a second identifier, so I\u0027ve dropped `PlatformConfigName` and a platform now pairs with a board record by its `Name`, the same way it names any other record.\nhttps://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/entity-manager/+/96318",
      "parentUuid": "94e78a13_8d46b369",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 23,
        "startChar": 39,
        "endLine": 23,
        "endChar": 44
      },
      "revId": "4e13cf52e4d897c12703c573767f2caf4eb0bf7a",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "cd7df825_2995c06b",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 17
      },
      "lineNbr": 23,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002395
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-27T17:01:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "@andhsieh@nvidia.com, I suggest not dropping `PlatformConfigName`. In my opinion, if different platform needs to name a device on a Board differently we can add a new Board config per each platform since for this requirement a Board loses a right to define the config for the devices on it (since it is platform specific) and such device configs just don\u0027t belong to a Board config that is platform agnostic.",
      "parentUuid": "8caddcf6_48878a14",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 23,
        "startChar": 39,
        "endLine": 23,
        "endChar": 44
      },
      "revId": "4e13cf52e4d897c12703c573767f2caf4eb0bf7a",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
