      "writtenOn": "2026-10-27T17:01:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "@andhsieh@nvidia.com, we can also explore possibility of making PlatformConfigName an array to handle such use case. \n\nRemoving PlatformConfigName would force nvidia-gpu service (consumer of this config) to have dependency on Platform config to obtain the name of the device to use on D-Bus. In my opinion we should avoid that, Platform confing and this nvidia-gpu config are two independent configs and nvidia-gpu service should not have dependency on Platform config to obtain the name of the device to use on D-Bus. I still prefer keeping `PlatformConfigName` here and use it to associate this nvidia-gpu config to MCTP device (EID).\n\nThis config is just for nvidia-gpu service. A config for other service (pldm, spdm, etc) would also need a way to associate its config to MCTP device (EID) and using `PlatformConfigName` is good example to do that I think.",
      "parentUuid": "dd518969_e71f1d8f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 47,
        "startChar": 35,
        "endLine": 47,
        "endChar": 44
      },
